  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Decision\\n\\n**The `1.2.0`-line behaviour does not apply. The observation-cursor behaviour that governs this workspace is the post‑1.2.0 (`ORD-BOOT-0`) state-change-feed cursor shipped in Ordarium `1.3.1`: an opaque, filter-independent, *always-present* durable commit position, capability-gated and **fail-closed** (`INVALID_CURSOR`) on an invalid/foreign/restored cursor.**\\n\\nThe only cursor the integration actually *exercises today*, however, is the ordinary state-subject **list-pagination** cursor — not the observation cursor. Details below.\\n\\n## Why the 1.2.0 commentary is out of scope\\n\\nThe single in-repo document that talks about this is `docs/release-commentary-1.2.0.md`. It is deliberately self-scoping:\\n\\n> \\\"…it predates the incremental state-change feed, so it has no notion of a change-feed cursor and no cursor-invalidation failure. **Anything here applies only to the 1.2.0 line.**\\\"\\n\\nSo it documents the *alternative* (or rather the *pre*-change-feed) behaviour: no observation cursor at all, therefore no cursor-invalidation failure. It is explicitly historical and superseded.\\n\\n## Why the workspace is NOT on that line\\n\\nThe integration is pinned to Ordarium `1.3.1",
